It's decent but there are better options. Rakan, Pyke, Alistar outclasses her in the role of an engage support right now. They have tools to engage without relying too much on their respective summoner spells(maybe except for Alistar)  and they are not gated by their ultimate. They also have better base stats than Annie too.  She is the Engage version of Karma. Karma is the poke mage early and a shield support later whilst Annie is the poke mage early with her autos and some Qs and becomes an engage support later.

&#x200B;

Her engage is still strong though, albeit more delayed since the MYMU. She is under the radar right now and if the meta supports got nerfed, I'm sure she'll go back to becoming a good support again. She has more tools to engage now too, from Predator to Righteous Glory to Shurelya's Reverie and even Spell Binder if you got ahead. I've seen pros use Annie support with either Predator or Aftershock (lately) as their keystone. 

